1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
What is that?

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Tournaments have been held
in each of the last 15 years,

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
and, in all that time,
East Gorteau has yet to lose.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,000
They are now
on their third representative,

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
who is a five-time reigning champion.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Hmm. So then if I defeat this champion,

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
I'll be the best in the world?

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
A fitting end to this diversion.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Call them.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
[opening theme music playing]

11
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

12
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
[singer singing in English]

13
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
[singer singing in English]

15
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

16
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
CHECK X AND X MATE

17
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,000
the King has spent this time
in his palace,

18
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
defeating masters of shogi,
go, and other board games.

19
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,000
has just been summoned.

20
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
[sniffs]

21
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
You and I will play Gungi,

22
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
but I'm learning the rules now,
so you must wait.

23
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,000
[Komugi] Oh! I'm so sorry.

24
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
and I'm always saying the wrong thing.

25
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
[grunts]

26
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
[wind blowing]

27
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
[King] Okay, I got the gist of it.

28
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
What's the matter now?

29
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
[Komugi] Gosh.
That was pretty embarrassing.

30
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Like I said, I'm not that smart.

31
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:08,000
My folks are always yelling at me.
[sniffles]

32
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
[King] Just start.

33
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Right!

34
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
It's a real honor to play against you.

35
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
No, not at all.

36
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
So would you please
announce your moves for me?

37
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
I can't help but keep them open,
not while I'm playing,

38
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:46,000
but if that's unacceptable,
I can try…

39
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
[Komugi] Soldier four-four-one.

40
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
[wind blowing]

41
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
[Knuckle] So you can't reach him at all?

42
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,000
[Gon] No. His phone must be off.

43
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:17,000
I guess we did agree that
he'd always initiate contact,

44
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
so it's not all that surprising.

45
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,000
[Meleoron] The hell?

46
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Why does that guy look like he was born
in the wrong decade?

47
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,000
By the look on his face,

48
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:36,000
he's the kind of guy
who's always looking for a fight.

49
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,000
makes it look like he's scared
and suspicious of everything.

50
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:49,000
I doubt he'll ever give me
a chance to explain myself.

51
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Whatever I say will
probably just go in one ear

52
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
and come out the other.

53
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
I hate to say it, Gon,

54
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,000
but my first impressions
are super bad.

55
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
[dog whimpers]

56
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
[Meleoron] Eh?

57
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
[whimpering]

58
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Hey, what's going on?

59
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
[Knuckle] Beats me.
It's just a pack of strays, I guess.

60
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
But they're all wearing collars.

61
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
[Shoot] What he's not telling you
is that he's been feeding

62
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:28,000
all the animals left behind
due to the sorting,

63
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
even though it cuts into his sleep.

64
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Eh, shut up! Not all of 'em.

65
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:35,000
We don't have time to waste on that crap.

66
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Don't you think I know that?

67
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
So I gave up on the ones
that had no chance.

68
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Aren't you proud of me?

69
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Some were just skin and bones
and refused to eat what I offered 'em.

70
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
And then there were the stupid, loyal ones

71
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
who refused to leave their homes
even after I unchained 'em.

72
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:56,000
What's so bad about saving
the ones that want the help?

73
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
[voice breaking] Tell me that!

74
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
You wanna get smacked in the head? [sobs]

75
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
[Meleoron] Hmph.

76
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,000
That's not enough
to change my opinion of him.

77
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Well, maybe a little.

78
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,000
And now shinobi, seven-eight-two.

79
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,000
That's checkmate.

80
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
GENERAL
SHINOBI

81
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:46,000
[King] A strategy to stack a bow
as a basis for attack and defense,

82
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:49,000
a typical Yagura castle.

83
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
Nothing particularly striking
in that strategy.

84
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
The opening array
was by the book as well…

85
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,000
We will play another.

86
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Yes! I would be happy to.

87
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
[Gungi piece clatter]

88
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:20,000
[Komugi] Cavalry, eight-eight-one.

89
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
That's checkmate.

90
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,000
I'm surprised. You're such a fast learner.

91
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Congratulations, supreme leader.

92
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
[King]
That's enough. Go get some rest.

93
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,000
Huh?

94
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
[sniffles] There's no need.

95
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
I'm fine to keep playing if you want to.

96
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,000
I've played gungi for three days
without sleep before.

97
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
I have a rematch.

98
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Once I've finished with him,
you'll have your turn.

99
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Oh.

100
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:59,000
Then I will rest.
I'm sure it will do me good.

101
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
There are several strategies,

102
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
but it's basically the same
as all the other games.

103
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:25,000
A few more rounds, and I'll be able
to make her play for real.

104
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Once I do,
I'll be able to observe her rhythm.

105
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
ARCHER

106
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,000
[dramatic music playing]

107
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
[narrator] In the palace,
the King continues to play

108
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:05,000
against the Gungi master,
hoping to hone his skills.

109
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
[Morel] Deep purple.

110
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
[inhales]

111
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,000
[grunts]

112
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,000
so in the event that the enemy retaliates,

113
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
I can maintain 50 of them at once,

114
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
and they're highly effective.

115
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
One big advantage to doing it this way

116
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:09,000
is that En can't differentiate
between one of these and a human being.

117
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
But chimera ants are still ants,

118
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
so Neferpitou won't leave the King's side.

119
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
So restricting the movement
of the royal guard

120
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
should be a piece of cake.

121
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,000
The only question is,
how will the King respond?

122
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:44,000
If he's impulsive,
it'll be harder to anticipate his actions.

123
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:52,000
But as long as they keep
these coming, we're fine.

124
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:00,000
[intense music playing]

125
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,000
Hey, it's been a while.

126
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
It's really good to see you.

127
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
[scoffs] He's leveled up.

128
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:11,000
The air around him
feels totally different.

129
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
Knuckle's A.P.R. is gone.

130
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
if something bad had happened.

131
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,000
If A.P.R. is gone,

132
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
I'll beat you down first…

133
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:54,000
and then the pompadour will be next.

134
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:58,000
[Morel] There must be a reason
he's so confident.

135
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
We'll see about that.

136
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:11,000
If that ability is to exorcise Nen,
we're in big trouble.

137
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:36,000
I was really hoping that our strategy
would be effective against the King.

138
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:43,000
However, if he can exorcise Nen,
this is a golden opportunity.

139
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
If I neutralize him now,

140
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Knuckle and Shoot's strategy
could still work.

141
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:56,000
I have to do it.
I can't deactivate deep purple,

142
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,000
so I'll have to get by
on my remaining aura.

143
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
[grunts]

144
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Now you're the one who's it for a change.

145
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
I'm what? What are you saying?

146
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,000
[dramatic music playing]

147
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,000
[rumbling]

148
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,000
Huh?

149
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Where the hell am I?

150
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Looks like a savannah.

151
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Did he teleport me?

152
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
If this is his new ability,

153
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
a different chimera ant
is the Nen exorcist.

154
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
You have eight hours.

155
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Hey, didn't you hear
what I just said to you?

156
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,000
You can't leave here
without touching me first!

157
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Those are the rules!

158
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:40,000
I guess I could chase you,
but I'd still never be able to catch you,

159
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,000
so might as well take my time.

160
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
[groans]

161
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
[Leol] Cheetu activated his ability.

162
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,000
I don't know what it does,

163
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
but they won't be back
for another eight hours.

164
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
[dramatic music playing]

165
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
[Morel] The backdrop's a wall.

166
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,000
It looks like I'm in some kind of space

167
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,000
separated from the real world,
just like he said.

168
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,000
Seems to be about the size
of a baseball field.

169
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:38,000
for me to deactivate Deep Purple
from within this space?

170
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,000
It's too risky to try.

171
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Huh?

172
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
[Morel] I can't deactivate Deep Purple,

173
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,000
at least, not yet.

174
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Well, well.
Are you finally ready to start?

175
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
You're just wasting time.

176
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
You can't destroy the hourglass or wall.

177
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
It's like I said.
There's only one way out,

178
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:57,000
and if you don't catch me,
you're gonna be stuck here.

179
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,000
[Morel] His ability was clearly influenced

180
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:07,000
by Knuckle's Hakoware,
Chapter Seven Bankruptcy, so…

181
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:25,000
Looks like there's more to this ability.

182
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
This might take a while.

183
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:36,000
[groans] Are you messing with me?

184
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,000
[snoring]

185
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:42,000
[growls]

186
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
[Morel chuckles]

187
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Go ahead. Lose your temper.

188
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,000
It's starting to look

189
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:50,000
like you don't understand
your own ability.

190
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:54,000
This is not a battle of speed.

191
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,000
This is a contest of wills.

192
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:02,000
[running footsteps]

193
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:05,000
[Knov] Deep purple is still activated…

194
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,000
so the plan continues.

195
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:16,000
[tense music playing]

196
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,000
A man in a suit
with black hair and glasses.

197
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
[Leol] Anyone else?

198
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,000
[Flutter] No. Just him,

199
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
along with the figures in white.

200
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
[Leol] Those white figures

201
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,000
are probably nothing
but ordinary soldiers.

202
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,000
But it is possible

203
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,000
that the true leader is concealed
among them.

204
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,000
No matter what,

205
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:47,000
I can't let anyone see my ability,

206
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:51,000
and Hirin can't go out after
exorcising the Nen from Cheetu.

207
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
and after that, he might even decide

208
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
to come out there and play himself.

209
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
We'll be there to protect him,
of course,

210
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
but you never really know
what might happen.

211
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Our preference is for the King
to remain inside

212
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:27,000
[Neferpitou] Go give Leol a hand.

213
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,000
[Welfin] Right.

214
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,000
[Bloster] As you wish.

215
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
Hmm.

216
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,000
[Shaiapouf] This player is a true master.

217
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:14,000
[Komugi] Two-eight-two, fort.

218
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Impossible.

219
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:39,000
There were only 144 moves,
start to finish.

220
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:44,000
This could only have happened
if she predicted my game from the start.

221
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,000
[Neferpitou] A storm is brewing.

222
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:00,000
[narrator] The girl's strength
upsets the King,

223
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:12,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

224
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:33,000
[Gon] Next time, "Doubt and Hesitation."

225
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
[Gon and Killua] Please, go easy on me.

226
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,000
-[Gon] Clack!
-[Killua] Whack!

227
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
-[Gon] Klickety-clack clack!
-[Killua] Bam!

228
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:46,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
